! After-the-seat, rows 26 to end (half B): shape audit

Source: bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem, `#/after-the-seat` (lines 545-621). Fence: line 98 (ruling) and X0 (line 535).
Read-only. No test ran. Code checked at the cited lines.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/table`>>

!! Table

| row | class | reason |h
| W11 | BEHAVIOUR | Four alarm probes on Keyhive 0.3.0-alpha.1; the test only measures (`packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/face-chain-substrate.probe.test.ts:1-20`). Writes no bytes. |
| W17 | UNSURE | "Face switching on one device". Canon says the switch ACT persists, vessel-private, never on the wire (`api/pono/session-contract.mem:116`, `:258-270`). No switch-act code exists yet (only a comment, `packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-face-presentation.ts:21`). Ruling at road line 98 says the face-switch act lands before the live test with two operators. Settle: the act row's field list and whether any CID or address derives from it. |
| W19 | BEHAVIOUR | A browser-weld walk (test road); the row names no format. |
| W20 | BEHAVIOUR | Guards by name for burned names. The browser one is an IDB upgrade that deletes `boot-invite-burned` (`packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-vessel-identity.ts:119`); moving the guard edits no live store. Note: that delete is itself a tolerant migration, and the bake makes it dead code. |
| W22 | BEHAVIOUR | `composeCasTransits` combines two fetch transports (`packages/lararium-node/src/node-cas.ts:171`); a fetch by CID leaves the CID alone. `walkInvite` option takes a carried invite string (`open-browser-vessel.ts:265`, `:600`). |
| W23 | BEHAVIOUR | A CI job and a vitest-config guard test. |
