| F2 | BEHAVIOUR | Moves compose sites onto `resolveSurfaceRecipe` / `mountSurface`; pool key is in memory. |
| F6 | BEHAVIOUR | Slice four moves the daemon kernel into the holder. Slice three (Repo move, sealed writes) already stands (row text), so the rest format is already fixed. Holder messages ride ports, not storage. Low confidence: I did not read the holder code. |
| F8 | BEHAVIOUR | Test assertions only ("burned-name guard assertions in `lar-wire.test.ts`"). |
| F9 | SHAPE (moderate) | "The vessel-wide selector retires". The selector rests in a persisted store: IDB `ACTIVE_PERSONA_STORE` (`browser-vessel-identity.ts:101`) and the node's active-persona index (`wearPersona`, `lararium-mesh/src/persona-vault.ts:59,187`; `lararium-node/src/sealed-acts.ts:409`). Retiring it after the bake leaves that store in founded vessels; the only ways out are a delete-on-upgrade reader (the pattern at `browser-vessel-identity.ts:119`) or a re-genesis. Also the road lists "the switch" in train O1 before "TWO HEARTHS" and ruling line 98 puts it before the live test. |
| H1 | UNSURE | `host door` / `host answer`. The introduction and sealed answer shapes already stand (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/introduction.ts:1-45`). The hosting store keeps no introduction rows (`lararium-node/src/hosting-store.ts:1-40`); a door that "shows what waits" needs a place to rest them. Settle: whether that new store is sealed and outside CID-bearing bytes (then BEHAVIOUR; it adds a class, no old reader). |
| H3 | BEHAVIOUR | Opens the shut `grant`/`claim` arms (`lararium-node/src/socket-sorter.ts:11,28`) over the landed signed grant (`walker-grant.ts`). Sorter logic. |
| H4 | BEHAVIOUR | `strangersHeld` is already a field of the hosting act (`lararium-mesh/src/hosting-delegation.ts:54,112,123`); the dial wires an existing field. |
| H7 | BEHAVIOUR | One doctrine line (canon prose). |
