<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-id-less-rows`>>

!! The id-less rows
The row between B6 and X1 is `X0b`, and it does carry an id. It needs no new id. The true id-less rows are the ten bullets after X5 (first words: "The boot's order holds four named reds nobody wrote", "Wikis-first writes: `meme promote` holds no in-wiki path", "Whether the browser shore serves its worn face plane", "Fleet gathering must batch", "No SES or Compartment realm gate", "Operator power reaches no browser vessel", "Observer-local hardening by silence", "The bag-tier reader takes the hearth's manifest alone", "The declared tier's share gate", "A startup module inside the VM"). I read each as BEHAVIOUR or a question; none names a byte. They need ids only if a train will cite them.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/move-before-the-bake`>>

!! Move before the bake
# F9 (selector retires): stride-2-floor. It retires a persisted store (see table). Landing it after X0 leaves the store in a founded vessel. Cure: retire it with the switch slice, before X0.
# W17 and the switch act it needs (also B2, F9): UNSURE, but ruling line 98 already says "the face-switch act ... ALL land before" the two-operator live test. Shelving them after the seat contradicts that ruling. Controller decision: either move the switch slice to stride-2-floor, or amend line 98. If the act row stays vessel-private and sealed (`session-contract.mem:116`), the shape risk is low, since no old version exists to read.
# X0b: its instrument should run once before X0. Findings that rename rows go into the bake.

<<~/ahu>>

